    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440-a2">

                <pb facs="0410" n="336" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg336"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 3, 30
                    papers.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Rev. Mr.
                        Descombaz.</head>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 1, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President:</hi> I have received your touching and
                    sympathetic address to the President of the United States, and shall experience
                    a sad satisfaction in transmitting it to him. The horrible crime which has
                    called him to succeed to the first martyr in the list of our Presidents will
                    make him especially thankful for your sympathies and your prayers.</p>
                <p>The deep emotion which our national mourning has everywhere excited, and
                    particularly in France, proves that the assassin who has deprived us of the
                    precious counsels of President Lincoln has given to him the immortality of the
                    martyr, and forever placed before us this rare example of Christian courage and
                    patriotism.</p>
                <p>I beg you, sir, to accept for yourself and your reverend colleagues the
                    assurances of my deep veneration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Pastor Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Descombaz,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">President of the Evangelical Alliznce of
                        Lyons.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
